From e0bcfc084ea423dec00cdd01000300d0c0a0a077 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 20:17:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/82] sunxi: h713: one HY310 base defconfig and a fragment
 per role

Six defconfigs described one board. They agreed on 53 lines -- the SoC,
the DRAM block the board's own boot0 declares, the console, the eMMC, the
power lines -- and disagreed on 28. Every DRAM fix therefore had to be
made six times, and the one that was not, was not: the comment above
CONFIG_DRAM_CLK announced the bench board's 624 MHz above a 792 for a year
because six copies is five chances to miss one.

Now the board is hy310_defconfig and what a build is *for* is a fragment
in configs/fragments/, merged with scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m and
make olddefconfig. Six roles: release, installer, netboot, netboot_gate,
felmmc, host.

The base is the shipping build minus the three lines that make it the
shipping build -- the power gate, the environment file, the boot command
-- and not the intersection of the six, which is what it looked like it
should be. The reason is that a merged fragment subtracts reliably and
adds unreliably. Kconfig lowers a symbol when its dependencies stop being
met, but not when the thing that merely raised it goes away, so a base
without the USB gadget left ANDROID_BOOT_IMAGE, CMD_FASTBOOT and their
neighbours at n and the fragment that switched the gadget on did not bring
them back. With the gadget in the base the three roles that do not want it
switch it off and the dependent symbols follow by themselves. Four do not
-- CMD_BIND is implied, ANDROID_BOOT_IMAGE and USB_MUSB_PIO_ONLY are
defaulted, CIRCBUF is selected -- and those four are named in the
fragments, with the reason.

Proven, not asserted: for each of the six, base + fragment through
merge_config.sh -m and olddefconfig produces the same .config as the old
defconfig did, symbol for symbol. The only difference is the device tree,
which is the point of the commit before this one, and CONFIG_OF_LIST,
whose default follows it. The script is umbau/work/E3b/prove-fragments.sh
and it needs no cross toolchain: config targets only.

Two things deliberately kept as they are. The installer's German boot
message is copied verbatim, because translating it is a text change and
this commit changes no build. And h713_probe_defconfig stays a base of its
own rather than becoming a role: it runs at 624 MHz on boards nobody has
measured, which is a board statement, not a role statement.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
